// Same racer at 03:00: sparse patrols, short witness and recognition ranges, slow civilian reports.
// Pursuit takes longer than 30 s on average (a patrol can still happen to be right there) and
// reinforcements arrive slower (ratios asserted in tests/police_scenarios.rs). The floor was 60 s
// until 2026-10-20: a patrol that watches a violation within recognition range (40 m at night) now
// engages at once (playtest row 34); measured mean 37.9 s, day 5.5 s.
(
    name: "police_night_core_speeder",
    seed: 100,
    time_of_day_h: 3.0,
    duration_s: 480.0,
    runs: 8,
    racers: [(district: Core, speed_factor: 2.0)],
    expect: [
        (metric: "pursuit_start_s", min: 30.0, max: 10000.0),
    ],
)
